{"severity":"error","file":"errors/duplicate_binder_5.march","start_line":7,"start_col":14,"end_line":7,"end_col":15,"message":"`x` is bound twice in the same parameter list or pattern.","code":"duplicate_binder","fix":null,"labels":[{"file":"errors/duplicate_binder_5.march","start_line":7,"start_col":11,"end_line":7,"end_col":12,"message":"first bound here"}],"notes":["A parameter list or a pattern binds each name once, so there is no single value this name could refer to.","Rename one of them, or write `_` for an argument you don't use. To require two values to be equal, bind two names and compare them in a `when` guard: `(x, x2) when x == x2 -> …`."]}
